{"dossier":"D08","entry_points":[{"sids":["arch/arm64/kvm/emulate-nested.c::triage_sysreg_trap"],"text":"Sysreg triage chooses local emulation, nested forward or fault from encoding, config, feature-forbid, nesting context and fine or coarse state."},{"sids":["arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/entry.S::__guest_enter","arch/arm64/kvm/handle_exit.c::arm_exit_handlers","arch/arm64/kvm/handle_exit.c::handle_hvc","arch/arm64/kvm/guest.c::kvm_arch_vcpu_ioctl_set_guest_debug"],"text":"Guest enter preserves host, defers on async, switches MTE and PAuth and returns via ERET; class dispatch routes exits; HVC counts and forwards; guest-debug validates mask."}],"exports":[{"sids":["arch/arm64/kvm/emulate-nested.c::kvm_inject_nested_sync","arch/arm64/kvm/emulate-nested.c::kvm_inject_nested_sea","arch/arm64/kvm/inject_fault.c::kvm_inject_sync","arch/arm64/kvm/inject_fault.c::pend_sync_exception","arch/arm64/kvm/inject_fault.c::kvm_inject_undefined","arch/arm64/kvm/inject_fault.c::inject_undef64","arch/arm64/kvm/inject_fault.c::inject_undef32"],"text":"Nested and fault injection forward sync syndromes, build SEA aborts with EASE async routing, and handle undef width-aware targeting EL1 or EL2."},{"sids":["arch/arm64/kvm/hypercalls.c::kvm_smccc_call_handler"],"text":"SMCCC trap resolves filter, serves version, features, pvtime, vendor and time locally, delegates RNG, else PSCI; resumes on results, exits on hypercall, preloads failure for power."},{"sids":["arch/arm64/kvm/psci.c::kvm_psci_call"],"text":"PSCI dispatcher allow-checks then selects legacy or modern by guest version; unknown versions report unsupported."}],"extracts":["ced86e4d16b366d4877637d3257c000c651132ca9ae094dc023878ddf39c736a","dd0f89676ac9d26e0e634db4f73361c9f974a56789c0d78d38a5701530ba38cf","eef415cd9a3918733dc4f88392ab4346fe5e13c3ccbcf94b8c1cfc44d51f0960"],"gpl_spec":"PASS","hazards":[{"sids":["arch/arm64/kvm/emulate-nested.c::triage_sysreg_trap","arch/arm64/kvm/hypercalls.c::kvm_smccc_call_handler","arch/arm64/kvm/psci.c::kv